# Environment variables.
#
# The glob, not a bare `.env`, because the dangerous files are the sidecars an
# editor leaves behind: .env.swp holds the buffer -- every secret in plaintext --
# and .env.bak is what `sed -i.bak` drops next to the original. On 2026-08-26 a
# .env.swp appeared as UNTRACKED on the production host, one careless
# `git add -A` away from being committed to a public repository.
#
# Keep the negation if a .env.example is ever added, so the template stays
# tracked while nothing carrying real values can be.
.env*
!.env.example

# Editor and merge leftovers -- same reasoning, applied generally.
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.orig
*.rej

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Virtual environment
.venv/

# PyCharm
.idea/

# Database
*.db

# Docker
postgres_data/
# subagent-driven-development scratch (review packages, briefs)
.superpowers/
